course: dictionary
lesson: 15149
title: Schoolbook
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A schoolbook is a book you use for lessons at school. It can be a textbook, which teaches a subject, or an exercise book, which you write in and practise. Schoolbook is a noun, and its plural is schoolbooks.
explain: Context helps you work out a word's meaning. «Mia packed her maths schoolbook and her pencil case into her satchel.» Mia puts the book into her bag for school, so a schoolbook is a book for lessons. Ask: what kind of book would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Stories from long ago give clues too. «In the old schoolroom, there were only a few schoolbooks, and each one was precious.» Few and precious tell you that schoolbooks were rare and valued long ago.
fact: A schoolbook is a book used for lessons at school.
fact: A textbook and an exercise book are both kinds of schoolbook.
fact: The plural of schoolbook is schoolbooks, meaning more than one.
fact: Children often carry their schoolbooks in a satchel.
fact: In stories from long ago, schoolbooks were few and precious.
exercise: «Sam put his schoolbook in his satchel before he left for school.» What is a schoolbook? | A lunch box | A book about the sea | A kind of bag | *A book used for lessons at school
exercise: «The old schoolbooks were few and precious.» What does precious suggest about the schoolbooks? | Cheap and easy to lose | *Very valuable and treasured | Noisy and cracked | Wet from the rain
exercise: Which of these is a schoolbook? | A satchel | A pencil case | *An exercise book for maths | A football
test: Find and copy the plural of schoolbook from this sentence: «Lena stacked her schoolbooks on the desk.» | Lena | *schoolbooks | schoolbook | desk
test: Alice tries to remember what she learned from her lessons and schoolbooks. What are schoolbooks in this sentence? | *Books used for lessons at school | Puzzles from the school fair | Things you eat at lunch | Stories about princesses
exam: Which word best completes this sentence? «A textbook and an exercise book are both kinds of ____.» | satchel | desk | *schoolbook | lesson
